        ":question/id": "16f98c04-c89a-5e4f-bf27-ed015bececed",
        ":question/problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}+2tan⁡x.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(tan⁡x)={sec}^{2}⁡x.$ Applying these formulas, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}+2tan⁡x) \\\\  & =1\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(tan⁡x) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}})+2({sec}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{\\sqrt{x}}+2{sec}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      }
    },
